// Hydrothermal district veins: seraphhorizons' SmallerDeposits switch (README.md "Ore cells",
// docs/oregen.md "Hydrothermal districts"). Read by Ore/Game/DistrictVeinSizes.cs; the rules are
// Ore/Core/DistrictVeins.cs. Sizes come from config/ore-sizes.json (small / typical / large).
//
// - veinsPerMetal: per district, the most veins (ore shoots and ladder veins) of each sized metal
//   not in keepCount; its ore in further veins, and in horsetail lenses, is not placed. #435 asked
//   for about 5–10 per metal per district (Interesting Ore Gen makes 40–80 of tin alone).
// - keepCount: the metals only districts provide, which keep every vein IOG makes (still sized).
// - gradeAllowance: ore per block over the poorest grade's; nine blocks in ten are the poorest
//   away from a fault's rich bands. 1.25 since #863 (1.15 before): the pack's units put the richer
//   grades further above poor (rich 2.3x and bountiful 3.3x poor's, from 1.7x and 2.3x), so the
//   rich bands' share over poor is about 1.4 times what it was (0.1 x 2.5 x 1.4 = 0.35).
// - bandFloor, bandBelowSeaLevel: a sized vein is a band of heights between bandFloor and sea
//   level less bandBelowSeaLevel, so it lies in rock wherever the land is above the sea.
{
  "veinsPerMetal": 8,
  "keepCount": ["gold", "silver", "platinum", "chromium"],
  "gradeAllowance": 1.25,
  "bandFloor": 4,
  "bandBelowSeaLevel": 6,
}
